fix(machine-setup): read brew linkage labels that break a load

Brew files a dependency's removed library, simdjson's in sd:10895,
under `Broken dependencies`, not `Missing libraries`, and --test
exits 1 on every label, undeclared dependencies too. The check read
only `Missing libraries` and took exit 1 as no answer, so it hid the
broken formula behind a no-answer failure and failed healthy runs.

Class: reading `brew linkage --test` output by one label and the
exit code. Fixed in each instance: the label parse, the item print
(only the two load-breaking blocks), the exit-1 rule (an answer with
a keg heading and no Error line), the tests' fixtures, the README.

Closes: sd:10895
